  "_meta": {
    "schema": "drug_alias/v1",
    "purpose": "Map any Chinese drug name read off a pill box to a canonical generic code.",
    "rules": [
      "A code is an entity, not a molecule family.",
      "★ resolve_drug() matches `drugs` ONLY. A combination product resolves to None — it is a different entity from any of its components and must go to the caregiver for review (spec §10.1).",
      "Combination products live in `combinations` with their `components`. safety.check() expands them, so 缬沙坦 + 诺欣妥 is correctly caught as a duplicate generic.",
      "No alias may appear under two codes. tests/test_data_integrity.py enforces this.",
      "Never add an alias you have not seen on a real box or in a national formulary.",
      "TODO: ~100 single codes today. Spec DoD requires >=300 entries covering all of evals/boxes. Grow this from the boxes you buy, not from a model."
    ],
    "updated": "2026-08"
  },
